    "text": "ABSTRACT The menstrual cycle is increasingly described as a “vital sign of the female body,” with the literature suggesting cycle- related brain and behavioral changes. With growing interest in the effects that the menstrual cycle has on the brain, body and mind, characterizing what constitutes healthy cycle- related change has become a central goal of behavioral neuroendocrinology. Considering the epistemological importance of research in behavioral neuroendocrinology for shaping our understanding of cycle- relate",
