    "text": "The long tradition of menstrual cycle research in human biology highlights the crucial importance of considering environmental variations, particularly sources of stress, to characterize adap- tive variation in the “normal” menstrual cycle (Clancy 2023; Vitzthum et al. 2021). Similarly, critical feminist/queer science scholars have also emphasized the importance of socio- cultural situatedness as enacting sources of stress on the body that vary by intersectional positionality (Bowleg 2008; Krieger 1999), as cultura",
