    "text": "Acute and chronic stressors arising from gendered experience act both directly and indirectly on the ovarian system. For instance, changes in behavior related to menstrual restriction (e.g., reduc- tion in physical or social activity during menstruation) or body dissatisfaction can contribute to cyclical variability through diverse effects of stress systems (Pletzer et al. 2021; Schliep et al. 2015). Lack of access to menstrual products and clean facil- ities is associated with a greater risk of infection, which, i",
