    "text": "According to the International Federation of Gynecology and Obstetrics, a normal menstrual cycle should occur every 24–38 days, with cycle length variation not exceeding 9 days and menstrual bleeding not exceeding 8 days (Munro et al. 2018). Normative variation of cycle length primarily impacts the follicular phase, reviewed in (Schmalenberger et al. 2021). Age has been associated with variation in endocrine profiles (Ellison 1996) and cycle length (Lenton et al. 1984) with a higher proportion of normally cycling i",
