    "text": "Epidemiologists have also been interested in the variation of menstrual patterns (timing and frequency) and reproductive hormones because of their associations with breast cancer (Mumford et al. 2012; Whelan et al. 1994; Terry et al. 2005). As a result, hundreds of studies have compared hormones between women with and without breast cancer; between women with dif- ferent risk factors, such as reproductive events, diets, and physical activity levels; and between women living in populations with different breast can-",
