    "text": "menstrual cycle include vaginal bleeding, basal body temperature (BBT), cervical fluid or mucus, and urinary levels of LH, and estradiol, progesterone, and their metabolites (21). BBT is measured upon waking at approximately the same time each day (23). It is approximately 0.5 °F (0.3 °C) lower in the follicular than the luteal phase (21, 22). After ovulation, increasing progesterone raises BBT until 1–2 days before menses, when BBT falls. Daily BBT tracking can be used to confirm ovulation retrospectively. Changes",
