    "text": "You might need tests, such as an ultrasound scan, to find out what's causing your period pain. If a condition is found, treating it will help. For example, if you have fibroids, you may be given medicine to shrink them or have surgery to remove them. If you have pelvic inflammatory disease, you'll usually need antibiotics. Page last reviewed: 18 March 2026 Next review due: 18 March 2029 Home NHS App Manage NHS profiles About us Health A to Z Find my NHS number Other NHS websites Report an issue with the",
