    "text": "There is no cure for PCOS, but treatments can improve quality of life, assist with fertility, reduce the risk of endometrial hyperplasia and/or endometrial cancer and help prevent long-term cardiovascular events. Seeking health care early to manage symptoms of PCOS can help women protect their health and well-being during and beyond their reproductive years. Healthy lifestyle behaviors, including healthy eating and physical activity, are important for all women with PCOS, even if they do not lead to weight loss.",
